# How to contribute

## Virtual environment
This repo use `poetry` to manage Python dependencies and virtual environments. After you run `poetry install`, a python virtual environment will be created at `.venv` under repo root with all dependencies installed. You can activate the env by

```bash
# To activate
poetry shell

# To run (no need prefix `poetry`)
python <path-to-entrypoint.py>

# To deactivate
exit
```

or if you prefer to using vanila Python:
```bash
# To activate
source .venv/bin/activate

# To run
python <path-to-entrypoint.py>

# To deactivate
deactivate
```
It's handy to develop after entering this virtual environment as it also contains all development dependencies. Also running `python <path-to-entrypoint.py>` is faster than running `poetry run entrypoint` so better for frequent testing.

## Dependency management
Dependencies are defined in `pyproject.toml` file. There are two sections for dependencies:

* `[tool.poetry.dependencies]`: for production
* `[tool.poetry.dev-dependencies]`: for development

To add a new dependency, simply add a new line in the corresponding section and run `poetry lock`. Or you can use

```bash
# For prod dependencies
poetry add <package-name>

# For dev dependencies
poetry add <package-name> -G dev
```
which will automatically update `pyproject.toml` and `poetry.lock`.

Please always commit your `poetry.lock` file to make sure everyone is using the same version of dependencies.

## Pre-commit
 `pre-commit` to lint and format code, so before contributing make sure to install `pre-commit` by:
```bash
source .venv/bin/activate  # Or use `poetry shell`
pre-commit install
```
Then `pre-commit` will run automatically before every commit.

## Type annotations
Please add type annotations to all functions and classes following the [official docs of Python 3.10](https://docs.python.org/3.10/library/typing.html). This is benenifical for high code qualit, easy reading and data validation using [Pydantic](https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/).
